       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum daily dose for adults (3,200 mg/day). At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose is unlikely to add much pain relief.\n\nThese are the usual options within the label:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the maximum for this indication.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily:** 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed for pain:** no more than 3,200 mg/day, and usually much less.\n\nLower doses and shorter courses are generally preferred, and taking it with food helps with GI tolerance.\n\nIf 1600 mg was meant as a **single dose** (for example, 1600 mg/day divided differently) or if you meant a different drug, let me know. Tell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it."
